DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_6C4C_DDDD';
<p>6c4c_dddd</p> <h4>Two-Point Test Cross Problem</h4><p>A test cross is a way to explore the relationship between genes and their respective alleles. It is a useful tool for genetic mapping and deciphering the inheritance of traits. Specifically, a two-point test cross examines two (2) genes at the same time to learn about their assortment in gamete formation.</p><p>A standard two-point test cross involves crossing a heterozygous organism for both genes with an organism that is homozygous recessive for both genes</p> <p>For this problem, a test cross using a fruit fly (<i>Drosophila melanogaster</i>) heterozygous for two genes was conducted to understand their genetic interactions.</p><h6>Characteristics of Recessive Phenotypes</h6><p><ul><li><strong><span style="color: #9d362b;">Gene B</span></strong> is related to the '<span style="color: #9d362b;"><i>bumpy</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #9d362b;">Gene B</span> has a skin texture that is not smooth, but rough with small bumps all over.</li> <li><strong><span style="color: #006b73;">Gene P</span></strong> is linked with the '<span style="color: #006b73;"><i>prickly</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #006b73;">Gene P</span> is covered with sharp bristles, giving it a spiky texture.</li> </ul></p><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 2px solid black;"><tr><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Phenotype</span></th><th colspan="2" align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Genotypes</span></th><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Progeny<br/>Count</span></th></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">bumpy, prickly</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe3df; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">b</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #c9f3f9; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">p</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">20,758</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">bumpy</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe3df; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">b</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #006b73;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">6,583</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">prickly</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #9d362b;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #c9f3f9; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">p</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">6,738</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;"><i>wildtype</i></span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #9d362b;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #006b73;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">20,921</span></td></tr><tr><th colspan="3" align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">TOTAL =</span></th><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">55,000</span></td></tr></table><p>The resulting phenotypes are summarized in the table above.</p> <h6>Question</h6> <p>With the progeny data from the table, <strong>calculate the genetic distance between the two genes,</strong> expressing your answer in centimorgans (cM)</p>
PROMPT_6C4C_DDDD
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_1';
<sup>(20,758 + 20,921)</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = <sup>41,679</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = 0.7578 = <strong>75.78 cM</strong>
LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_2';
<sup>(6,583 + 20,758)</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = <sup>27,341</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = 0.4971 = <strong>49.71 cM</strong>
LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_3';
<sup>(6,583 + 20,921)</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = <sup>27,504</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = 0.5001 = <strong>50.01 cM</strong>
LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_4';
<sup>(6,583 + 6,738)</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = <sup>13,321</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = 0.2422 = <strong>24.22 cM</strong>
LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_5';
<sup>(6,738 + 20,758)</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = <sup>27,496</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = 0.4999 = <strong>49.99 cM</strong>
LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_5
$choice_6 = <<'LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_6';
<sup>(6,738 + 20,921)</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = <sup>27,659</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = 0.5029 = <strong>50.29 cM</strong>
LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CHOICE_6
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CORRECT_1';
<sup>(6,583 + 6,738)</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = <sup>13,321</sup>/<sub>55,000</sub> = 0.2422 = <strong>24.22 cM</strong>
LITERAL_6C4C_DDDD_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5, $choice_6);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->buttons\}
END_TEXT
ANS($answer->cmp);

ENDDOCUMENT();
